      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Exercise: image registration (ECC) - burst align + stack denoise\n\nA handheld burst never lines up: every frame is shifted/rotated a little, so averaging the frames directly GHOSTS (bottom row). Here three misaligned noisy frames are synthesized from one photo (cv2.getRotationMatrix2D about three different centers -> cv2.warpAffine, + the 'Add Gaussian noise' subgraph), then each is registered back onto the reference with 'CV Find Transform (ECC)' - direct intensity-based alignment, no keypoints. The recovered warp is applied with cv2.warpAffine using 'INTER_LINEAR | WARP_INVERSE_MAP' (pull the frame INTO the reference), and the aligned frames are averaged: the noise drops by ~sqrt(N) while the detail stays sharp. Compare the three PSNR readouts: single noisy frame < unaligned average (averaging still cancels noise, but the ghosting caps the gain) < aligned average, which wins by ~10 dB.\n\nFAILURE PATH (right): raw cv2.findTransformECC RAISES when it cannot converge - the curated node instead reports found=false and an identity warp, so a featureless frame flows through: the if/else picks the untouched frame and the workflow keeps running (a failed registration is a valid result, not an error)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
